# Notes

A literate file of its own module writes a type through another module's name like any file.

    module notes

    import geometry.shapes

The parameter, the result and the field are written through the module.

    widen(s: shapes.Shape) -> shapes.Shape = s match
        shapes.Circle(r) -> shapes.Circle(r + 1)
        shapes.Square(side) -> shapes.Square(side + 1)

    class Note(val shape: shapes.Shape)
